                <pb facs="0385" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/691: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the American Representation on the
                        Preparatory Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-24T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1928—12 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 25—5:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>24. My 20, March 24, 4 p.m. Cushendun’s letter handed me during final afternoon
                    session of Commission and came as complete surprise. Cushendun and Admiral Kelly
                    left immediately afterwards for London, so I had no opportunity to discuss
                    proposals or learn why they were presented here.</p>
                <p>We have declined to discuss matter with press and have taken the stand that
                    comment must come from Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
